DataLens — multi-tenant natural-language querying
=================================================

This distribution contains:

1. The `vanna` library (`src/vanna/`), derived from the upstream project at
   https://github.com/vanna-ai/vanna, Copyright (c) Vanna.AI, MIT licensed.

   Modified here. The substantive additions are the semantic layer
   (`src/vanna/semantic/`), the datasource registry (`src/vanna/core/datasource/`),
   the ranked retrieval index (`src/vanna/capabilities/index/`), the dashboards
   package (`src/vanna/dashboards/`), the billing plans (`src/vanna/core/billing/`),
   and the authentication primitives (`src/vanna/core/auth/`).

   The upstream `vanna.legacy` package -- the 0.x compatibility surface, roughly
   eleven thousand lines covering twenty-five vendor integrations -- has been
   removed. Nothing in this distribution imported it.

2. The DataLens application (`docker/vanna_app/`), which is a multi-tenant deployment
   of that library: control plane, accounts, billing, and the HTTP surface over
   them. Original to this repository, MIT licensed on the same terms.

3. Front-end assets (`frontends/`): the `<vanna-chat>` web component, the workspace
   page and the operator console.

See LICENSE for the terms, which apply to all of the above.

Third-party dependencies are declared in `pyproject.toml` and pinned in
`docker/requirements.txt`; each carries its own licence.
